1 Overview
**********

‘rl’ is the command-line interface for the rl programming language.  It
provides tools for running, checking, scaffolding, formatting, and
packaging rl source files, plus a package manager.

   Compiling to bytecode, transpiling to C, the interactive REPL, the
language server, the docs viewer, and the toolchain manager ship as
separate binaries: ‘rlc’, ‘rlt’, ‘rlrepl’, ‘rlsp’, ‘rldocs’, and ‘rlm’.


