8 print Command
***************

‘rl print FILE’ prints debug information for a ‘.rl’ source file.
Exactly one of ‘--tokens’, ‘--parser’, or ‘--ast’ must be given.

8.1 Options
===========

‘-t, --tokens’
     Print the token stream from the lexer.

‘-p, --parser’
     Print the parsed AST (before type checking).

‘-a, --ast’
     Print the type-checked AST.

8.2 Examples
============

     $ rl print script.rl --tokens
     $ rl print script.rl --parser
     $ rl print script.rl --ast


