9 package Command
*****************

‘rl package FILE’ packages a ‘.rl’ file into a self-contained binary.
The ‘.rl’ source text is embedded directly into the compiled output.

9.1 Options
===========

‘-o PATH, --output PATH’
     Output binary path.  Defaults to ‘program’.

‘--vm’
     Compile to ‘.rlc’ bytecode first and embed that (compressed)
     instead of the raw source text.

9.2 Examples
============

     $ rl package script.rl
     $ rl package script.rl -o myapp
     $ rl package script.rl --vm


