11 pm Command
*************

‘rl pm’ manages project dependencies: it downloads tarballs, verifies
SHA256 hashes, and links them into ‘deps/’.

11.1 Examples
=============

     $ rl pm install some-package
     $ rl pm list


File: rl.info,  Node: test Command,  Next: Examples,  Prev: pm Command,  Up: Top

12 test Command
***************

‘rl test FILE’ discovers ‘!#[test]’ functions and runs them with
setup/teardown hooks, reporting pass/fail/skip with a non-zero exit on
failure.

12.1 Options
============

‘--match PATTERN’
     Only run tests whose name, group, or register contains PATTERN.

‘-c CODE, --code CODE’
     Execute inline rl code instead of a file.

12.2 Examples
=============

     $ rl test tests.rl
     $ rl test tests.rl --match money


